### Program Overview

This program implements a Brill Tagger, a type of transformational rule-based tagger used in natural language processing (NLP). The Brill Tagger uses an initial tagger to assign an initial tag sequence to a text and then applies an ordered list of transformational rules to correct the tags of individual tokens. The program includes several predefined template sets and provides functionality to train and evaluate the Brill Tagger.

### Classes and Structs

#### Word Class

**Purpose**: Represents a feature that examines the text (word) of nearby tokens.

**Fields/Member Variables**:
- `json_tag`: A string representing the JSON tag associated with this class.

**Methods**:
