### Program Overview

This C++ program solves a problem related to finding the maximum difference between two elements in a sequence where the first element must be less than a given threshold `m`. The input consists of multiple test cases, each specifying a sequence of integers and a threshold value. For each test case, the program calculates and outputs the maximum difference found according to the rules described.

### Classes and Structs

The program does not define any classes or structs. All functionality is encapsulated within the `main` function.

### Global Variables and Standalone Functions

#### Global Variables

- `t`: Number of test cases.
- `n`: Length of the current sequence.
- `m`: Threshold value.
- `a`: Vector representing the sequence of integers.
- `p`, `q`: Indices used to track positions in the sequence.
- `M`: Variable to store the maximum difference found.

#### Standalone Functions

- `main()`: The entry point of the program, which handles reading input, processing each test case, and outputting results.

### Detailed Description

#### Main Function

