#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>

int main() {
    int t; // Number of test cases
    std::cin >> t;

    while (t--) {
        int n; // Length of the current sequence
        int m; // Threshold value
        std::cin >> n >> m;

        std::vector<int> a(n); // Vector representing the sequence of integers
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
            std::cin >> a[i];
        }

        int p = 0; // Index used to track positions in the sequence
        int q = 0; // Index used to track positions in the sequence
        int M = -1; // Variable to store the maximum difference found

        while (p < n && q < n) {
            if (a[p] < m) {
                q++;
                if (q >= n) break;
                M = std::max(M, a[q] - a[p]);
            } else {
                p++;
            }
        }

        std::cout << M << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

### Explanation

- **Global Variables**:
  - `t`: Number of test cases.
  - `n`: Length of the current sequence.
  - `m`: Threshold value.
  - `a`: Vector representing the sequence of integers.
  - `p`, `q`: Indices used to track positions in the sequence.
  - `M`: Variable to store the maximum difference found.

- **Main Function**:
  - Reads the number of test cases.
  - For each test case, reads the length of the sequence and the threshold value.
  - Reads the sequence into a vector.
  - Initializes indices `p` and `q` and sets `M` to -1.
  - Uses a while loop to find the maximum difference where the first element is less than `m`.
  - Outputs the maximum difference for each test case.
