This C++ program calculates the total number of direct and indirect orbits in a given satellite system. The input is a text file representing the orbital relationships between satellites and their central bodies, formatted as `CENTER)SATELITE`. The program reads this input, constructs a graph representation of the satellite system, and then computes the sum of distances from the central body (`COM`) to all other satellites.

